1
00:00:00,397 --> 00:00:02,277
[PHONE RINGING]

2
00:00:04,401 --> 00:00:06,401
- Answer the phone, Leonard.
- No.

3
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:09,030
[PHONE CHIMING]

4
00:00:09,198 --> 00:00:10,828
There. It went to voicemail.

5
00:00:17,456 --> 00:00:19,456
(Sheldon:)Aren't you going
to check your messages?

6
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:24,550
(Leonard:)- No.
- You have to check your messages.

7
00:00:24,713 --> 00:00:27,463
(Sheldon:)The leaving of a message
is one half of a social contract...

8
00:00:27,633 --> 00:00:30,343
(Sheldon:)...which is completed
by the checking of the message.

9
00:00:31,678 --> 00:00:34,768
(Sheldon:)If that contract breaks down,
then all social contracts break down.

10
00:00:34,932 --> 00:00:37,182
(Sheldon:)And we descend into anarchy.

11
00:00:38,811 --> 00:00:41,691
(Leonard:)It must be hell inside your head.

12
00:00:43,816 --> 00:00:45,696
(Sheldon:)At times.

13
00:00:46,944 --> 00:00:48,404
(Howard:)Guys, we have a code red.

14
00:00:48,570 --> 00:00:51,320
Code red, the hospital emergency alert?
The computer worm?

15
00:00:51,490 --> 00:00:54,740
Or the cherry-flavored soft drink
from the makers of Mountain Dew?

16
00:00:55,536 --> 00:00:58,036
(Howard:)I was going over the schematics
on my Zero-G Toilet...

